\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesu, priceless treasure,
\par Source of purest pleasure,
\par truest friend to me;
\par Ah! how long I have panted,
\par And my heart hath fainted,
\par Thirsting, Lord, for Thee!
\par Thine I am, O spotless Lamb,
\par I will suffer not to hide Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In Thine arm I rest me;
\par Foes who will molest me
\par Cannot reach me here;
\par Though the earth be shaking,
\par Every heart be quaking,
\par Jesus calms my fear;
\par Sin and hell in conflict fell
\par With their bitter storm assail me:
\par Jesus will not fail me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Hence, all fear and sadness,
\par For the Lord of gladness,
\par Jesus, enters in;
\par Those who love the Father,
\par Though the storms may gather,
\par Still have peace within;
\par Yea, whate'er I here must bear,
\par Still in Thee lies purest pleasure,
\par Jesu, priceless treasure!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

